Fix vdd_cpu regulator i2c address on RGB30

The tcs4525 buck regulator that powers the CPU is at i2c address 0x40
on the RGB30 (verified by i2cdetect: 0x1c is empty, 0x40 responds),
not 0x1c as the v1 dtsi says. With the wrong address, tcs452x driver
never binds, no vdd_cpu regulator exists, and arm_rockchip_cpufreq
refuses to register any policies (correct behaviour - won't change
freq without matching voltage). Symptoms: CPU stuck at boot default
408 MHz (max is 1.8 GHz), empty /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpufreq/,
empty "clock rate" menu in EmulationStation system settings.

The address is already correct in rk3568-evb-rgb30-v2.dtsi but that
file gets included by rk3566-rgb30-v2-linux.dts which drops a bunch
of suspend/wakeup/power-key config we want to keep. Fixing the v1
dtsi in place keeps all of v1's suspend and power-key behaviour and
only changes the wrong hex digit.

Signed-off-by: James Pharaoh <james@pharaoh.uk>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3568-evb-rgb30.dtsi | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3568-evb-rgb30.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3568-evb-rgb30.dtsi
@@ -408,9 +408,9 @@
 &i2c0 {
 	status = "okay";

-        vdd_cpu: tcs4525@1c {
+        vdd_cpu: tcs4525@40 {
                 compatible = "tcs,tcs452x";
-                reg = <0x1c>;
+                reg = <0x40>;
                 vin-supply = <&vccsys>;
                 regulator-compatible = "fan53555-reg";
                 regulator-name = "vdd_cpu";
